author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 2400
acceptance_criteria: "An environment author can run a complete episode - reset, step, observe, score - through public SDK primitives alone, with no import from src/cli and no shelling out, demonstrated by a worked example under docs/examples; A stable episode identity spans every surface and process an episode touches, is recorded in the immutable stream, and groups a trajectory correctly when a session mixes CLI and MCP calls; The boundary between a pm-computed verdict and an author-computed reward is stated as a contract, with pm's side reproducible from recorded state and independently checkable; Observation cost is declared before the call and honoured, so a training loop can budget tokens per step without measuring empirically; The programme's own scale claim is proved on a generated corpus at the 100k and 1M points using the existing harness, reporting per-step latency and observation size rather than only assembly latency; Reproducibility is proved end to end: the same episode specification and seed produce byte-identical workspace state and an identical verdict across runs and across platforms; Every constituent item retains its capability parent and carries a typed edge to this epic, so the programme is traversable without moving ownership"
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: 88
